description: Docker and Compose conventions for the CIM database stack
globs: cim-database/**,**/Dockerfile*,**/docker-compose*.yml,**/docker-compose*.yaml
alwaysApply: false
---

# Containers

- Pass configuration with environment variables. Do not copy `.env` files or passwords into
  an image.
- The database image must keep PostGIS (see `cim-database/Dockerfile.citydbv4`). Do not
  switch it to plain PostgreSQL.
- Keep published ports consistent with the connection strings in use. The integrated stack
  exposes Postgres on host port `15432`.
- Run one process per container.
- Prefer the Compose files already in the repo over adding another orchestrator.
